)

The file named in the question is removed from every ranking.

*Flow questions (48).* Each question asks which file-to-file edges carry a behaviour, for example "How are user sessions stored in signed cookies?", and has two or three correct edges. A *dev* set of 23 questions (this repository's backend and Python service, plus `hackathon-starter`) was used to study mistakes while we designed the content-based pruner. A *held-out* set of 25 questions covers seven other repositories and was written before any content-based pruner variant was run on it. We confirmed with the independent import oracle that every correct edge really exists. Whether an edge truly carries the behaviour is the annotator's judgement, and the annotator also wrote the pruner.

== Evaluated Experimental Conditions

*Retrieval methods.* Each takes a question and returns ranked files. A random ranking is also included as a floor.

